"""Annual Report: production theme and component kit (approved mock v8, 58 pages, 430x830 card per page).

Ported from docs/annual/mock/_build/shell.py + build_v8_anjali.py (v3..v8 overrides merged into ONE final layer).
CLAUDE.md section 8: only the section content changes; never edit this to restyle a single report.
Pure strings, no I/O. The renderers (annual_report*.py) import it the way diwali_report.py imports diwali_assets.py.

HOW TO USE
  from annual_assets import document, card, tiles, chip, ...
  cards = [card(body_html, n, eyebrow, title, cls) for ...]       # one printed page each
  html  = document(''.join(cards), 'Annual Report - Anjali')       # complete standalone HTML, defs first in <body>
  Text arguments are trusted HTML (escape user text before passing). Month keys are 'YYYY-MM',
  tones are 'strong' | 'mixed' | 'careful'.
  card() cls: 'fx' (cover, note, thank-you: stay vertically centred), 'tt' / 'tt2' (tighter spacing for dense
  pages), 'gloss', plus any module class from scope().
  All cards must be direct children of one parent (document() does this): the corner art is chosen by
  position (nth-of-type), page 1 is the cover, page 2 the note, the last page the thank-you.

PAGE-NUMBER RULE
  card() prints the number in <div class="pgn">. The final CSS layer pins it in the footer: absolute, centred,
  11px, weight 400, #b9ae96, 18px from the bottom, the same spot on every page. Never style .pgn per module.

ADDING MODULE CSS SAFELY
  Never add a bare <style> to a card. Use scope(card_html, 'm2a', css): it prefixes every selector with
  '.m2a ' (or '.page.m2a' for selectors starting with .page) and tags the section, so the rules only reach
  that module's cards. Plain rules only (no @media / @keyframes inside module CSS).
"""
